                                             # The guest's boot id rides along: a (pid, start time) pair is unique only
                                             # WITHIN one boot, and the orphan registry must never match it against a later
                                             # incarnation of the same VM name. "boot=" with nothing after it means the id
                                             # was unreadable; the host then does not register the command.
                                             qd_ident_b=$(cat /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id 2>/dev/null)
                                             if [ -n "$qd_ident_s" ]; then printf 'start=%s boot=%s\n' "$qd_ident_s" "$qd_ident_b"; else printf 'gone\n'; fi"
